Learning Goals

By completing these three videos, the goal is to develop an understanding of:

What Generative AI is and how it differs from traditional AI and machine learning approaches.
What foundation models are and why they are useful.
How Large Language Models generate responses.
How Amazon Bedrock provides access to foundation models.
How to interact with models through prompts and APIs.
How prompt engineering can influence model responses.
How RAG can provide models with external information.
How embeddings and vector databases support semantic search.
How agents can perform multi-step tasks.
How guardrails can help control model interactions.
How AI applications can be monitored and evaluated.
How security and IAM apply to Generative AI applications.
How model selection affects performance, latency, and cost.
How these concepts fit together when designing AI applications on AWS.
